# Performance, Data, Config & Delivery

## Performance & data
- Paginate all list/collection endpoints; never return unbounded result sets.
- Avoid N+1 queries; batch or join. Index columns used in WHERE/JOIN/ORDER BY.
- Move expensive work to async jobs/queues when it would block user requests.
- Cache deliberately, with an explicit invalidation strategy.

## Concurrency & state
- Make shared-state access safe (transactions, locks, atomic operations).
- Assume concurrent execution; design idempotent handlers for retries/webhooks.

## Configuration
- All environment-specific values come from config/env, never hardcoded.
- Provide a documented `.env.example` listing every required variable (no real
  values). Code must run identically across dev/staging/prod given correct config.

## Git & delivery
- Small, focused commits. Conventional style: `feat|fix|chore|docs|refactor: summary`.
- Never commit secrets, `.env` files, build artifacts, or large binaries.
- Update docs and tests in the same change as the code they describe.
